# Unbound: Worlds Apart (PPSA03274) -- past the title screen and the intro cinematic to the
# first level's map load.
#
# Anchors are SECONDS from the first pad poll (src/input/pad.cpp:207-210 -- a bare number is
# seconds, 'f' is flips, 'p' is pad reads).
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV, AMD Radeon 8060S / STRIX_HALO) at 3840x2160,
# headless `tools/screenshot` frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, PROSPER_GUEST_ARGS=-force-gfx-direct,
# no render acceleration. Measured 2026-08-22 on master bb57d617.
#
# THE TITLE SCREEN'S PROMPT AND THE CINEMATIC'S PROMPT NAME DIFFERENT BUTTONS.
#
# The 4K title screen draws a lone `X` glyph, and CROSS is right for it. What follows is not
# another CROSS screen: the intro cinematic draws its own prompt, and it reads
#
#     "Press [] to skip"
#
# -- SQUARE. MEASURED: a cross-only ladder (110 presses, 330 s) reached the cinematic and then
# sat on it for the remaining 180 s with that SQUARE prompt still on screen. Adding SQUARE at
# t=78 skips it, and the first level loads 4 ms later.
#
# PROGRESS ORACLE IS THE FILE LOG, NOT PIXELS (PROSPER_FILELOG=1), because this title loses most
# of its presents to the #2932 wrong composite and a pixel read of one sample is unreliable. The
# oracle has a negative control, which is what makes it worth anything:
#
#   default route, no input, 120 s   -> last asset is  movies/screen_village_logo.mp4
#                                       NO mainmenubg.mp4, NO intro_01.mp4, NO normalvillage
#   this route, 330 s                -> movies/mainmenubg.mp4   t~3.5
#                                       movies/intro_01.mp4     t~7.0
#                                       /app0/normalvillage     t~78.0   <- the first level
#
# `normalvillage` is reproduced at t=78.01 on two independent runs, and it appears in the log
# immediately after the SQUARE press, on the same line group as the guest's own
# `sceAvPlayerSetTrickSpeed` call (NID av8Z++94rs0) -- i.e. the skip path. It is absent from
# every default run measured.
#
# WHAT THIS ROUTE DOES NOT DO: it does not produce a rendered level. After the map load the guest
# stays alive and the renderer keeps producing frames (flips 3146 -> 7812, rendered frames
# 3258 -> 12811 over the following 250 s), but 175 of the 178 samples after the load are a flat
# two-tone clear with exactly half the pixels non-black. That is the #2932 wrong composite, not
# this route, and it is why the title is still rung 2. Phase 3 below is written for the world
# that load implies; it has not yet had one to move through.

